Fall back to a real Application when makeApplication fails, instead of a bad cast.

SYMPTOM
    Launching a guest activity in a proxy process -- notably Chrome's sandboxed
    renderer bind -- can fail in BActivityThread.handleBindApplication because
    LoadedApk.makeApplication throws. The fallback then did:

        application = (Application) packageContext;

    packageContext is a ContextImpl, never an Application, so the cast threw
    ClassCastException and the process died with:

        java.lang.RuntimeException: Unable to makeApplication
          at BActivityThread.handleBindApplication
        Caused by: Unable to makeApplication - all fallback attempts failed
        Caused by: ClassCastException: android.app.ContextImpl cannot be cast to
                    android.app.Application

    This is reproducible from the OnePlus CPH2605's data_app_crash DropBox entries
    (2026-09-10, processes co.tdevs.duplika:p0 and :p1) and is the unresolved
    "Defect B" named in docs/chrome-stay-signed-out-android15-investigation.md.

FIX
    Reuse the class's own createApplicationWithFallback(), which retries the guest
    Application and finally builds a minimal android.app.Application with a base
    context. The bind then completes instead of aborting the process.

diff --git a/Bcore/src/main/java/top/niunaijun/blackbox/app/BActivityThread.java b/Bcore/src/main/java/top/niunaijun/blackbox/app/BActivityThread.java
--- a/Bcore/src/main/java/top/niunaijun/blackbox/app/BActivityThread.java
+++ b/Bcore/src/main/java/top/niunaijun/blackbox/app/BActivityThread.java
@@ -451,7 +451,7 @@
                     Slog.w(TAG, "Creating minimal application context as fallback");
                     try {
                         
-                        application = (Application) packageContext;
+                        application = createApplicationWithFallback(applicationInfo);
                         if (application == null) {
                             Slog.e(TAG, "Even package context is null, this is critical");
                             throw new RuntimeException("Unable to create application context");
